# Package sources for EOL Debian releases (bullseye and older)
#
# Debian 11 went EOL at the end of August 2026. Since then its security
# packages are disappearing from the live mirrors while bullseye-security is
# NOT yet on archive.debian.org (which still ends at buster). During that move
# the package index names versions whose .deb is already gone, and which of
# the two you get depends on the CDN node that answers - so `apt-get install`
# fails with a pile of 404s, intermittently.
#
# snapshot.debian.org serves a frozen point in time, so index and pool come
# from the same moment. `Check-Valid-Until` has to go off because a snapshot's
# Release file is deliberately old.
#
# Consequence to be aware of: security updates are frozen at this date. These
# images are pinned to an old distribution anyway (Odoo 12/13 need a Python
# that newer Debian no longer builds), so there is nothing newer to get here.
# Raise the date when such an image is rebuilt on purpose.
#
# Must be repeated per build stage - every FROM starts from the base image
# again. The apt_cacher image carries the same pin in its own Dockerfile
# (SNAPSHOT_DATE); keep the dates in sync when raising one.
RUN printf '%s\n' \
      "deb http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/20260824T000000Z bullseye main" \
      "deb http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/20260824T000000Z bullseye-updates main" \
      "deb http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian-security/20260824T000000Z bullseye-security main" \
      > /etc/apt/sources.list && \
    rm -f /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.list /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.sources && \
    printf 'Acquire::Check-Valid-Until "false";\n' > /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99snapshot
